// The frame round every page of Spell UI (epic `mockup` T39, T55):  Spell UI's docs site's look, its side bars floating.
// - The drawer:  the site's navigation, a card its button hides and shows.
// - Above each page its app menu:  the drawer's button and where you are;  in its middle the page's family as a switch,
//   Usage | Examples | API | Theming, as the editor's Run | Edit;  at its end the page's own links (Fomantic's original,
//   report a bug), the theme menu and the contents' button;  before them the site's search, which `/` and Cmd / Ctrl+K
//   focus:  every page, component, attribute and section (`<ui-docs-search>`, its search file written by
//   `yarn site:check --all`), its links the site's own addresses (`base="/"`).
// - Beside the page its contents, a card headed by the page's title, which its ✕ or that button closes.
// - No row of tabs under the menu:  they're the menu's switch, and a page's sections are in its contents.
<ui-defaults>
	<ui-page-layout floating drawer-hides />
</ui-defaults>

main layout is a page layout
	to draw its app menu
		<app-menu>
			<site-nav-button slot="start" />
			<site-breadcrumbs slot="start" />
			<site-tabs appearance="header" />
			<docs-search slot="end" base="/" />
			<site-links slot="end" report="https://github.com/spell-app/spell-ui/issues/new?title={title}" />
			<theme-menu slot="end" show="theme" compact />
			<site-nav-button slot="end" toggles="right" icon="list ul" />
		</app-menu>
	to draw its page menu
		// nothing:  the page's family is the app menu's switch
	to draw its right sidebar
		<toc>
			<site-nav-button slot="tools" toggles="right" icon="close" />
		</>
